					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13837047#post-4804800</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13837047/scp-5762#post-4804800</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2020 19:50:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TheShutteredEye</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3764997</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Honestly, I'm okay with a shallow piece.</p> <p>A problem I have with the current trend of SCPs is that there's not too much room for outside interpretation. Series I, while lacking much of the emotional depth and narrative complexity that's par-for-the-course nowadays, was good in that the simple concepts could allow really anyone to engage with it. This one has&#8230; room to breathe, if you will.</p> <p>However, I would have liked a little more interaction between Brey and the bot, and the characterization of the bot seemed a tad too shallow, But overall, the story is nice and concise.</p> <p>No vote.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
